#### Optimal 1

::: {.form-next}
The table carries `g` only to remember a half-filled column. Eliminating it leaves `f[n] = 2f[n-1] + f[n-3]`, derived in the callout above, with `f[0] = 1`, `f[1] = 1`, `f[2] = 2`. A step reads `f[n-1]` and `f[n-3]`, so three variables replace the array: `a, b, c = b, c, (2c + a) mod M`. That is what you submit for `n ≤ 1000`. The two-state bug, overwriting `g` before `f` has read it, cannot happen here because `g` is gone.
