## Pattern 2: include / exclude {#sec-dpi-p2}

**From steps to choices.** In Pattern 1 every position is visited and the only question is *how* we arrived. Now each item is a **decision** — take it or leave it — and taking one item forbids its neighbour. The animation shows the decision being made at every house.


**Recognise it.** A sequence of items, each either **taken or skipped**, with a constraint between neighbouring choices ("no two adjacent", "taking $x$ forbids $x \pm 1$"). Maximise the total.

::: {.callout-important title="Template"}
$dp[i]$ = best total using only the first $i$ items. Item $i$ is either **skipped**, giving $dp[i-1]$, or **taken**, giving $a_i + dp[i-2]$ (its neighbour must be skipped). So $dp[i] = \max(dp[i-1],\ a_i + dp[i-2])$. If the constraint is on **values** rather than positions, first bucket the items by value and run the same DP over the value axis.
:::

**Complexity.** $O(n)$ time, $O(1)$ space (plus $O(\max a)$ for the value-axis version).

