#### Recursion

::: {.form-next}
`go(r, c)` is the number of ways from cell `(r, c)` to the bottom-right corner. A step goes down, `go(r+1, c)`, or right, `go(r, c+1)`. Those paths share no continuation, so the counts add. An obstacle, or a step that leaves the grid, is 0 paths. The goal itself is 1 path: you are already there. The answer is `go(0, 0)`. On a 6×6 grid the tree is hundreds of calls per cell, because every route into a cell repeats the work below it.
:::

