**6. [M] (coding)** Count binary strings of length $n$ with no two consecutive 1s, using two states (ends in 0 / ends in 1).

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
$z_i$ = strings ending in 0, $o_i$ = ending in 1. $z_i = z_{i-1} + o_{i-1}$, $o_i = z_{i-1}$. The total is $F(n+2)$.

::: {#9631f058 .cell execution_count=153}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def no_two_ones(n):
    z, o = 1, 1
    for _ in range(n - 1):
        z, o = z + o, z
    return z + o

for n in range(1, 15):
    assert no_two_ones(n) == sum("11" not in "".join(t) for t in product("01", repeat=n))
```
