## Further reading

- [Erickson, *Algorithms*, ch. 3: Dynamic Programming](https://jeffe.cs.illinois.edu/teaching/algorithms/book/03-dynprog.pdf): "smart recursion", with a careful treatment of choosing subproblems.
- [Laaksonen, *Competitive Programmer's Handbook*](https://cses.fi/book/book.pdf), ch. 7: dynamic programming for contests, including LIS, grid paths and edit distance.
- [CP-Algorithms: Introduction to dynamic programming](https://cp-algorithms.com/dynamic_programming/intro-to-dp.html): memoisation vs tabulation on Fibonacci, and the classic first problems.
- [Wikipedia: Optimal substructure](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optimal_substructure): the property that makes "best answer from best sub-answers" correct.
- [Wikipedia: Bellman equation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bellman_equation): Bellman's principle of optimality, where the name and the idea come from.
- [CP-Algorithms: Fibonacci numbers](https://cp-algorithms.com/algebra/fibonacci-numbers.html): the matrix form of a linear recurrence, used for the $O(\log n)$ tiling form.
- [Wikipedia: Memoization](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memoization): caching a function's results, the top-down half of Lesson 2.
